# Create PR

Use this only when the user invokes `@create-pr` with a GitHub issue id, after implementation. Do not use it to plan or code. In a fresh chat, derive the slug from `git diff` / `git log` against `main` and the issue id.

Do not run `dotnet build` or `dotnet test` unless the user asks. CI covers that. In the PR notes, say verification was left to CI. Mark a checklist item done only when you can assert it without a full test run.

## 1. Inputs

- Issue id is required. `12` and `#12` are the same. Use `12` in the branch and `#12` in the PR body.
- If this checkout is for a different issue, stop. Do not switch worktrees to force the PR.
- Base branch is `main` unless the user names another.
- Title: `#<id> - <short summary>`. Derive the summary from the change. Keep an explicit user title, but keep the `#<id>` prefix.

## 2. Branch name

`<id>-<slug>`. Slug is lowercase kebab-case, at most five words, from the work that landed (`8-refill-dates`). No `feature/` prefix.

If the user gives a full branch name, use it.

## 3. Commit and update

Stay on this worktree. Never `git checkout main` here.

1. `git fetch origin`
2. If the branch is only `<id>`, rename it with `git branch -m <id>-<slug>`.
3. Merge `origin/main` into the feature branch when it is behind. Do not check out `main` in this worktree.
4. Commit changes that belong in this PR. Stash unrelated dirty files so they are not pushed.
5. Run Bugbot (§3a) before push.
6. `git push -u origin HEAD`

Do not force-push `main`.

## 3a. Bugbot before push

On the committed branch diff, launch one Bugbot subagent (`subagent_type: bugbot`, description `Bugbot`, not in the background). Prompt:

```text
Full Repository Path: <absolute repository path>
Diff: branch changes
```

- No findings → push and open the PR.
- Findings → show them and wait. Do not auto-fix. Continue only if the user says to proceed, or after they ask for fixes, you commit, and Bugbot is run again.
- If Bugbot fails, ask whether to proceed without it. Do not skip it silently.
- Note the Bugbot result in the PR body.

## 4. PR body

```markdown
## Summary
<what changed and why, in a few sentences>

## Related issues
Closes #<id>
```

Use `Closes #<id>` only when every acceptance criterion is met. Otherwise use `Refs #<id>` and leave the issue open (`github-ticket-flow`).

## Notes

- Build and tests were not run locally; CI validates.
- Bugbot: <no findings | proceeded with N findings after user confirmation>

Mention a migration or a docs update when this branch has one.

## 5. Open

```powershell
gh pr create --base main --head <branch> --title "#<id> - <summary>" --body-file pr-body.md
```

Delete `pr-body.md` after `gh` returns the URL. If `gh` is unavailable, give the compare URL and the same markdown.

## 6. Cleanup

After the PR exists:

1. Confirm `git status` has no leftovers from this flow.
2. If this folder is a sibling worktree (`PillDue-<id>`), call `move_agent_to_root` on the primary repo, then from there `git worktree remove "<path>"`.
3. Delete the local branch if it is fully pushed (`git branch -d`). Do not delete `origin/<branch>` or `main`.
4. Report the PR URL.

Do not clean up if PR creation failed. Do not remove the primary checkout.
